IMPORT prelude

-- Bills of Lading Act 1992 (Singapore) -- which shipping documents the Act covers (s 1), who is the lawful holder of a
-- bill of lading (s 5(2)), when rights of suit against the carrier pass to a holder or consignee (s 2), when that person
-- takes on the contract's liabilities too (s 3), and when a bill is conclusive evidence of shipment (s 4).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/BLA1992.txt. The deposit says it "incorporates
-- all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021" and came into operation on 31 December 2021; the latest amendment
-- annotated in the body is 5/2021 (on s 5(1)).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0100 in ../../../requirements.jsonl: Tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario
-- has asked a sharper question yet. The Act is six sections long, so the whole of its operative text is encoded. Not
-- encoded: the short title (s 6), the extended meaning of "identified" in s 5(3) beyond a comment, and the Hague-Visby
-- Rules which s 5(5) leaves untouched (they live in the Carriage of Goods by Sea Act 1972, not retrieved here).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Bills of Lading Act 1992 -- shipping documents`

§§ `1 -- the documents the Act covers`

-- s 1(1): the Act applies to "(a) any bill of lading; (b) any sea waybill; (c) any ship's delivery order".
-- s 1(2): a bill of lading "(a) do[es] not include ... a document which is incapable of transfer either by indorsement or,
-- as a bearer bill, by delivery without indorsement; but (b) subject to that, do[es] include ... a received for shipment
-- bill of lading".
-- s 1(3): a sea waybill is "any document which is NOT a bill of lading but (a) is such a receipt for goods as contains or
-- evidences a contract for the carriage of goods by sea; and (b) identifies the person to whom delivery of the goods is to
-- be made by the carrier".
-- s 1(4): a ship's delivery order is "neither a bill of lading nor a sea waybill" but contains an undertaking "(a) given
-- under or for the purposes of a contract for the carriage by sea ... and (b) ... by the CARRIER to a person identified in
-- the document to deliver the goods ... to that person".
--
-- The three definitions are a cascade: each is tried only if the earlier ones fail. So a document headed "bill of lading"
-- that cannot be transferred is, on the text's own terms, not a bill of lading at all, and falls to be tested as a sea
-- waybill. And a delivery order counts only if the undertaking is the carrier's.
DECLARE DocumentKind IS ONE OF
    `a bill of lading`
    `a sea waybill`
    `a ship's delivery order`
    `a document outside the Act`

DECLARE ShippingDocument HAS
    `is in the form of a bill of lading` IS A BOOLEAN
    `transferable by indorsement or as a bearer bill` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a received for shipment bill` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a receipt containing or evidencing a contract of carriage by sea` IS A BOOLEAN
    `identifies the person to whom the carrier is to deliver` IS A BOOLEAN
    `contains the carrier's undertaking to deliver to an identified person` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the document` IS A ShippingDocument
GIVETH A DocumentKind
DECIDE `the kind of document` IS
    IF `the document`'s `is in the form of a bill of lading` AND `the document`'s `transferable by indorsement or as a bearer bill`
    THEN `a bill of lading`
    ELSE IF `the document`'s `is a receipt containing or evidencing a contract of carriage by sea` AND `the document`'s `identifies the person to whom the carrier is to deliver`
         THEN `a sea waybill`
         ELSE IF `the document`'s `contains the carrier's undertaking to deliver to an identified person`
              THEN `a ship's delivery order`
              ELSE `a document outside the Act`

GIVEN `the document` IS A ShippingDocument
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Act applies to the document` IF
    NOT (`the kind of document` `the document` EQUALS `a document outside the Act`)

§§ `5(2) -- the holder and the lawful holder of a bill of lading`

-- s 5(2): the holder is "(a) a person with possession of the bill who, by virtue of being the person identified in the
-- bill, is the consignee ...; (b) a person with possession of the bill as a result of the completion, by delivery of the
-- bill, of any indorsement of the bill or, in the case of a bearer bill, of any other transfer of the bill; (c) a person
-- with possession of the bill as a result of any transaction by virtue of which he would have become a holder falling
-- within paragraph (a) or (b) had not the transaction been effected at a time when possession of the bill no longer gave a
-- right (as against the carrier) to possession of the goods", "and a person shall be regarded ... as having become the
-- LAWFUL holder ... wherever he has become the holder of the bill in GOOD FAITH".
-- s 5(3): "identified" includes identification "by a description which allows for the identity of the person ... to be
-- varied" after issue (not modelled: the flag below simply records that the person is the identified consignee).
-- s 5(4): the Act still operates where the goods "(a) cease to exist after the issue of the document; or (b) cannot be
-- identified (whether because they are mixed with other goods or for any other reason)".
DECLARE Claimant HAS
    `the document kind` IS A DocumentKind
    `has possession of the bill` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is the consignee identified in the bill` IS A BOOLEAN
    `took the bill by a completed indorsement or bearer transfer` IS A BOOLEAN
    `took the bill by such a transaction after it was spent` IS A BOOLEAN
    `became holder in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the bill was spent when he became holder` IS A BOOLEAN
    `took under arrangements made before the bill was spent` IS A BOOLEAN
    `got the bill back on a rejection of goods or documents` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is an original party to the contract of carriage` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is the person to whom delivery is to be made` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the goods have ceased to exist or cannot be identified` IS A BOOLEAN
    `takes or demands delivery from the carrier` IS A BOOLEAN
    `makes a claim against the carrier under the contract` IS A BOOLEAN
    `took or demanded delivery before the rights vested` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the claimant` IS A Claimant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is the holder of the bill` IF
        `the claimant`'s `has possession of the bill`
    AND (    `the claimant`'s `is the consignee identified in the bill`
         OR  `the claimant`'s `took the bill by a completed indorsement or bearer transfer`
         OR  `the claimant`'s `took the bill by such a transaction after it was spent`)

GIVEN `the claimant` IS A Claimant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is the lawful holder of the bill` IF
        `is the holder of the bill` `the claimant`
    AND `the claimant`'s `became holder in good faith`

§§ `2(1), (2) -- when rights of suit pass`

-- s 2(1): a person who becomes "(a) the lawful holder of a bill of lading; (b) the person who (without being an original
-- party to the contract of carriage) is the person to whom delivery of the goods to which a sea waybill relates is to be
-- made ...; or (c) the person to whom delivery of the goods to which a ship's delivery order relates is to be made ...
-- shall ... have transferred to and vested in him ALL RIGHTS OF SUIT under the contract of carriage as if he had been a
-- party to that contract".
-- s 2(2): where, when a person becomes the lawful holder, "possession of the bill no longer gives a right (as against the
-- carrier) to possession of the goods" (a spent bill), no rights pass "unless he becomes the holder ... (a) by virtue of a
-- transaction effected in pursuance of any contractual or other arrangements made before" the bill was spent; "or (b) as a
-- result of the REJECTION to that person by another person of goods or documents delivered ... in pursuance of any such
-- arrangements".
--
-- Nothing here turns on whether the goods still exist (s 5(4)): that flag is deliberately not read.
GIVEN `the claimant` IS A Claimant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the spent-bill bar does not apply` IF
        (NOT `the claimant`'s `the bill was spent when he became holder`)
    OR  `the claimant`'s `took under arrangements made before the bill was spent`
    OR  `the claimant`'s `got the bill back on a rejection of goods or documents`

GIVEN `the claimant` IS A Claimant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `rights of suit vest in the claimant` IF
    CONSIDER `the claimant`'s `the document kind`
    WHEN `a bill of lading` THEN `is the lawful holder of the bill` `the claimant` AND `the spent-bill bar does not apply` `the claimant`
    WHEN `a sea waybill` THEN `the claimant`'s `is the person to whom delivery is to be made` AND (NOT `the claimant`'s `is an original party to the contract of carriage`)
    WHEN `a ship's delivery order` THEN `the claimant`'s `is the person to whom delivery is to be made`
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `2(3), 3(2) -- a delivery order for part of the cargo`

-- s 2(3): rights under a ship's delivery order are vested "(a) ... subject to the terms of the order; and (b) where the goods
-- to which the order relates form a part only of the goods to which the contract of carriage relates, shall be CONFINED to
-- rights in respect of the goods to which the order relates". s 3(2): the liabilities likewise "exclude liabilities in
-- respect of any goods to which the order does not relate".
--
-- The Act says this only of a ship's delivery order; it is silent for the other two documents.
GIVEN `the kind` IS A DocumentKind, `the document covers only part of the cargo` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Act confines rights and liabilities to the goods in the document` IF
        `the document covers only part of the cargo`
    AND `the kind` EQUALS `a ship's delivery order`

§§ `2(4) -- suing for someone else's loss`

-- s 2(4): where "(a) a person with any interest or right in or in relation to goods ... sustains loss or damage in
-- consequence of a breach of the contract of carriage; but (b) ... rights of suit in respect of that breach are vested in
-- another person, the other person shall be ENTITLED to exercise those rights for the benefit of the person who sustained
-- the loss or damage to the same extent as they could have been exercised if they had been vested in the person for whose
-- benefit they are exercised".
GIVEN `the claimant` IS A Claimant, `someone else with an interest in the goods suffered the loss` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the claimant may sue for the other person's loss` IF
        `rights of suit vest in the claimant` `the claimant`
    AND `someone else with an interest in the goods suffered the loss`

§§ `2(5) -- what happens to the original shipper's rights`

-- s 2(5): the transfer "shall EXTINGUISH any entitlement to those rights which derives (a) where that document is a bill of
-- lading, from a person's having been an original party to the contract of carriage; or (b) ... from the previous operation
-- of that subsection", "but ... shall be WITHOUT PREJUDICE to any rights which derive from a person's having been an
-- original party to the contract contained in, or evidenced by, a sea waybill and, in relation to a ship's delivery order,
-- ... to any rights deriving otherwise than from the previous operation of that subsection".
--
-- Endorse a bill of lading and the shipper loses its right to sue the carrier. Name a consignee on a sea waybill and the
-- shipper keeps it -- so under a waybill two people may hold rights of suit at once. An earlier holder of any document
-- loses the rights it took under s 2(1) when the next person takes them.
GIVEN `the kind` IS A DocumentKind, `rights have since vested in someone else` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an original party keeps its rights of suit` IF
        (NOT `rights have since vested in someone else`)
    OR  (NOT (`the kind` EQUALS `a bill of lading`))

GIVEN `rights have since vested in someone else` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an earlier holder keeps the rights it took under section 2` IF
    NOT `rights have since vested in someone else`

§§ `3 -- when the liabilities follow`

-- s 3(1): where s 2(1) operates and the person in whom rights are vested "(a) takes or demands delivery from the carrier of
-- any of the goods ...; (b) makes a claim under the contract of carriage against the carrier ...; or (c) is a person who, at
-- a time before those rights were vested in him, took or demanded delivery from the carrier of any of those goods, that
-- person shall ... become subject to the same liabilities under that contract as if he had been a party to that contract".
-- s 3(3): this is "without prejudice to the liabilities under the contract of any person as an original party".
--
-- Rights come with holding the document; liabilities come only with ACTING on it. A holder who never asks for the goods and
-- never sues holds rights without liabilities. And the shipper stays liable even after its rights have gone (s 2(5) with
-- s 3(3)).
GIVEN `the claimant` IS A Claimant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the claimant takes on the liabilities of the contract` IF
        `rights of suit vest in the claimant` `the claimant`
    AND (    `the claimant`'s `takes or demands delivery from the carrier`
         OR  `the claimant`'s `makes a claim against the carrier under the contract`
         OR  `the claimant`'s `took or demanded delivery before the rights vested`)

GIVEN `rights have since vested in someone else` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an original party remains liable under the contract` IF
    TRUE

§§ `4 -- a bill of lading as conclusive evidence of shipment`

-- s 4: a bill of lading which "(a) represents goods to have been shipped on board a vessel or to have been received for
-- shipment on board a vessel; and (b) has been signed by the master of the vessel or by a person who was not the master but
-- had the express, implied or apparent authority of the carrier to sign bills of lading, shall, in favour of a person who
-- has become the LAWFUL HOLDER of the bill, be CONCLUSIVE evidence against the carrier of the shipment of the goods or, as
-- the case may be, of their receipt for shipment".
--
-- Only a bill of lading, only a lawful holder, only against the carrier. A sea waybill's statements get no such force from
-- this Act.
GIVEN `the kind` IS A DocumentKind, `represents goods shipped or received for shipment` IS A BOOLEAN, `signed by the master` IS A BOOLEAN, `signed by a person with the carrier's authority` IS A BOOLEAN, `relied on by a lawful holder` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the bill is conclusive evidence of shipment against the carrier` IF
        `the kind` EQUALS `a bill of lading`
    AND `represents goods shipped or received for shipment`
    AND (`signed by the master` OR `signed by a person with the carrier's authority`)
    AND `relied on by a lawful holder`
